WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480
What if I told you that people are

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:07.240
getting rich by starting new businesses

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.400
and new side hustles despite having no

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.520
pre-existing social media following and

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.560
no money to buy ads or pay for

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.920
marketing. Seriously, it's kind of

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.520
crazy, but there are now new AI-powered

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.520
traffic algorithms that you can

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.000
piggyback off of. Because if we're just

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.880
being honest here, I reckon that the

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.680
true bottleneck holding most people back

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.640
from business success isn't that they

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.560
don't know how to start a business, it's

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.840
that they don't know how to market it to

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.400
make it successful. Because seriously,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.280
if you want to start a business, there

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.680
are plenty of videos here on YouTube,

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.800
including admittedly my own videos,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.680
that'll happily give you lots of ideas

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.920
for ways that you could start one or

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.920
start a side hustle, especially with AI

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:47.160
tools. For example, like me, you could

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.080
start an Etsy store and sell products.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.200
Or you could vibe code an app and make

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.920
subscription or affiliate sales. Or you

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.240
could start a faceless TikTok or YouTube

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.800
channel and make money from ads. But

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:58.920
here's the thing, most people aren't

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.480
stuck for ideas for businesses. Instead,

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.520
the part that they struggle with most is

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:04.640
traffic. How do you actually get people

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.400
to buy stuff like your t-shirts? I've

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:08.280
seen so many people not even try to

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.280
start a business because this question

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.040
is paralyzing them. How do you get

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:13.840
people to see your products? How do you

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:15.640
get people to watch your videos? And

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.600
it's a fair question because before

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.920
there were AI algorithms to piggyback

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.040
off of, popularity bias made getting

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.160
traffic extremely hard. And if you don't

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:26.240
know what that is, popularity bias, it's

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:28.640
just another way of saying that before

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.880
AI, all the big platforms like YouTube,

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.560
Google, Instagram, LinkedIn, Amazon,

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.720
TikTok, Etsy, all of them, would only

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:37.920
recommend contents or products that were

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:40.280
already popular. Like take Etsy for

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:41.800
example, previously, when you came here

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.720
and did a search for something, the

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.920
search results heavily favored stores

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:47.640
with thousands of pre-existing reviews,

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.520
which made breaking in as a new seller

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.640
very difficult. Because let's say that

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:54.160
you created a new Etsy print-on-demand

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.840
store selling fun t-shirt designs. Well,

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:58.520
since your store was new and it had no

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.480
reviews and no sales, Etsy wouldn't

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:02.440
recommend it to anyone, but you think

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.280
about it. Without Etsy recommending your

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:06.280
store to anyone, it meant then that it

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.039
also never had a chance to get those

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:09.679
reviews or to get those sales.

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:11.640
Essentially, it was an impossible

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:13.800
chicken and egg situation. Without

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:16.120
traffic, you can't get popular, but the

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.120
only way that you can get popular is if

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:20.080
you were given traffic. And so, you only

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:23.120
had two real ways to get around this

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.760
problem. One way was to already be rich

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.800
and to have a lot of money so that you

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:29.400
could spend it on paid ads to force

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:31.480
sales and force popularity. Or another

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.040
way was to already have a big social

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:35.320
media following yourself on one

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.959
platform, like say on Instagram, and

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:39.000
direct reach your followers to go and

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:41.959
watch your videos on other websites,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.280
like say YouTube, to force popularity on

00:02:41.959 --> 00:02:46.920
there. But now, everything has changed

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:49.480
because new AI traffic algorithms have,

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:51.880
in my opinion, made getting traffic much

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:54.360
easier, even if you are a new content

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:55.840
creator or you are a new store. And to

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.959
understand why, to keep things

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:00.200
interesting, let's use YouTube as our

00:02:57.959 --> 00:03:02.280
example this time since they recently

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:04.760
released a research paper confirming

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:06.880
that Google's AI is now integrated into

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:08.920
its recommendation algorithm. And this

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:10.840
has been making a huge difference. In

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:12.600
YouTube's old algorithm, if you released

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:15.200
a video on a new account with no

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:17.360
followers, it would get no views. So,

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:19.480
YouTube would not share it since it was

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:21.519
not popular. So, it would die

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:23.920
immediately. But now, when you release a

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:25.959
new video on a new channel, Google's AI

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:27.880
will use its artificial intelligence to

00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:30.760
scan your video. It will try to figure

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:32.440
out who out of their 2.8 billion users

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:34.280
might want to click on your video and

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:36.080
watch it. And it will select a small

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.680
group of test viewers, and it will put

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:39.880
that video in front of them in their

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.880
home page and video recommendations to

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:43.560
see if they will click on it or not.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:45.720
There is a name for this process, and

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.880
it's called test impressions. And here

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:50.000
is the crucial part. If during this test

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:52.560
phase, people scroll past your video and

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.880
don't click on it, YouTube's algorithm

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.520
will stop recommending it. But, if

00:03:54.880 --> 00:04:00.080
people from your test cohort do actually

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:02.080
click it and enjoy it, your video moves

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.320
up to the next phase. The AI will now

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:06.000
expand your test group to a bigger group

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.920
of people, and it will show your video

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.840
to these people recommending it to them

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.000
on their home page as a video that they

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.040
might like to watch. And if those people

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.280
click it and actually watch it, then the

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:18.280
AI algorithm will keep expanding it,

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:20.480
showing it to more and more people. And

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:23.720
this is why getting traffic is now well

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:26.120
and truly, in my opinion, on easy mode.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:29.520
Because YouTube's AI algorithm now does

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:32.280
this for every single video. Every video

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:34.240
now has a fair chance to go viral, and

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:36.440
it doesn't matter if you, the creator of

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.360
that video, has no social media

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:41.000
following. And it doesn't matter if you

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:42.960
have not paid for ads. Every video that

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:45.720
is now released on the platform has a

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:47.080
chance to go viral for free, which means

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:49.280
that starting a successful YouTube

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:51.560
channel is no longer gatekept to people

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:53.480
who already have a following or who can

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.400
pay for initial traffic. It's

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:56.880
game-changing. And actually, there is a

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.360
technical name for this type of

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:01.240
algorithm, if you're nerdy like me, and

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.240
it's called a multi-armed bandit

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:04.640
recommendation algorithm. TikTok, I

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.680
believe, was the first to really push

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:08.640
this out, and it worked because it's a

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:10.880
genius system. Because one of the

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:13.280
previous problems with the old algorithm

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:15.200
system of showing popular content or

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:17.000
popular products to people was that it

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:18.560
would be a bit fatiguing for users.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.760
They'd see the same products, the same

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:22.440
videos, or the same content creators

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:24.640
over and over again, and they'd get

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:26.720
bored. So, test impressions are a huge

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:29.400
win-win. They allow all the big content

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:32.919
platforms or marketplaces, like Etsy,

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:34.880
Instagram, X, TikTok, Amazon, Facebook,

00:05:32.919 --> 00:05:37.160
Google, all of them use their own

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:39.200
